@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+# OpenClaw local patch notice
+
+This package is a patched derivative of the official `@discord/embedded-app-sdk@2.5.0`, not the unmodified Discord release. Its version string remains 2.5.0; identify the derivative by the applied patch and package manifests.
+
+- Official package: https://registry.npmjs.org/@discord/embedded-app-sdk/-/embedded-app-sdk-2.5.0.tgz
+- Official SRI: `sha512-FNoe5PbSkoKEbqPubaBmq6tlEMOftMjR3gu55YrdrrKmBfKKM4i9P/Z+Zxl0RZdJcKviBwVcTyYMMPM/aGex/w==`
+- Official source commit: `14264eccbf9e68d5d58c1aadbc7579e003e0dce6`
+- Owner TypeScript migration patch SHA256: `17ec6e28c9109f6f234fa53f7c34f8872107c7579d5fb0c9dabb1724c47ca8d1`
+- SDK owner source patch is preserved alongside the downstream package patch in the maintaining repository; no generated code was hand edited to perform the migration.
+
+The owner-source migration rebuilds the package with exact Zod 4.6.6, replacing the embedded Zod 3 implementation. It preserves the tested enum fallback, command validation, generic declarations, and message/nonce terminal behavior. Zod diagnostic text/code and schema types can differ; this notice is not a claim of universal API compatibility. The existing Discord MIT notice and the exact Zod 4.6.6 MIT notice are included together in `LICENSE.md`.
+
+Remove this downstream patch only after an official upstream SDK or separately governed replacement provides the same embedded-parser correction, its real dependency graph and complete installed output pass the relevant consumer/security/Linux install-and-restore checks, and patch retirement is explicitly recorded. Reverting to the unpatched official package restores the old embedded-parser behavior and is not a security-equivalent rollback.
